---
import DocLayout from "../../components/docs/DocLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<DocLayout
  title="Configuration (.npkillrc)"
  description="Learn how to configure npkill with a .npkillrc file for custom defaults, profiles, and more."
>
  <h1>Configuration (.npkillrc)</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The <code>.npkillrc</code> file lets you configure npkill's default behavior,
    create custom profiles, and save your preferences so you don't have to specify
    them every time.
  </p>

  <h2>File Location</h2>
  <p>
    By default, npkill looks for <code>~/.npkillrc</code> in your home directory.
    You can also specify a custom config file with the <code>-c</code> flag:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code="npx npkill -c /path/to/my-config.json" />

  <h2>Configuration Options</h2>
  <p>
    The <code>.npkillrc</code> file uses JSON format. Here's a complete example:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "defaultProfile": "node",
  "directory": "~/projects",
  "sort": "size",
  "excludeHiddenDirectories": false,
  "showErrors": false,
  "noCheckUpdate": false,
  "profiles": {
    "webdev": {
      "description": "Frontend artifacts and build outputs",
      "targets": ["dist", ".next", ".nuxt", ".output", "build"]
    }
  }
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <h3>Available Options</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Option</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>defaultProfile</code></td>
        <td>string</td>
        <td>Profile to use by default (e.g., "node", "python")</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>directory</code></td>
        <td>string</td>
        <td>Default directory to start searching from</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>targets</code></td>
        <td>string[]</td>
        <td>Default target directories to search for</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>sort</code></td>
        <td>string</td>
        <td>Default sort order: "size", "path", or "last-mod"</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>exclude</code></td>
        <td>string[]</td>
        <td>Directories to always exclude from search</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>excludeHiddenDirectories</code></td>
        <td>boolean</td>
        <td>Whether to exclude hidden (dot) directories</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>showErrors</code></td>
        <td>boolean</td>
        <td>Whether to display error messages</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>noCheckUpdate</code></td>
        <td>boolean</td>
        <td>Disable update checks on startup</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>profiles</code></td>
        <td>object</td>
        <td>Custom profile definitions</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Custom Profiles</h2>
  <p>
    You can define your own profiles in the <code>profiles</code> section. Each profile
    needs a name, description, and list of targets:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "profiles": {
    "mystack": {
      "description": "My full-stack development artifacts",
      "targets": [
        "node_modules",
        "dist",
        ".next",
        "__pycache__",
        ".venv",
        "target"
      ]
    }
  }
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <p>Then use it with:</p>

  <CodeBlock code="npx npkill -p mystack" />

  <div class="warning">
    <i class="bx bx-error"></i>
    <div>
      Custom profiles with the same name as built-in profiles will override
      them.
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Priority Order</h2>
  <p>
    Options are applied in this order (later options override earlier ones):
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>.npkillrc file</strong> — Default configuration</li>
    <li><strong>CLI flags</strong> — Command-line arguments</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Options panel</strong> — Changes made in the TUI options panel (temporary)
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    This means you can set sensible defaults in your <code>.npkillrc</code> and override
    them when needed with CLI flags.
  </p>

  <h2>Example Configurations</h2>

  <h3>JavaScript Developer</h3>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "defaultProfile": "node",
  "directory": "~/dev",
  "sort": "size"
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <h3>Full-Stack Developer</h3>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "sort": "size",
  "profiles": {
    "fullstack": {
      "description": "Node + Python artifacts",
      "targets": [
        "node_modules",
        ".next",
        ".nuxt",
        "dist",
        "__pycache__",
        ".venv",
        ".pytest_cache"
      ]
    }
  },
  "defaultProfile": "fullstack"
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <h3>Game Developer</h3>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "directory": "~/GameProjects",
  "profiles": {
    "gamedev": {
      "description": "Unity + Godot build artifacts",
      "targets": [
        "Library",
        "Temp",
        "Obj",
        "Build",
        ".godot",
        ".import"
      ]
    }
  },
  "defaultProfile": "gamedev"
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <h2>Validation</h2>
  <p>
    If your <code>.npkillrc</code> file contains invalid JSON or unknown options,
    npkill will show a warning and continue with default settings.
  </p>
</DocLayout>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .warning {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.3);
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .warning i {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-warning);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
</style>
